🎯 **What:** The testing gap addressed
The strrchr function was missing tests in the kernel sys/lib/string.c tests. This adds comprehensive test coverage.
Note: Fixed duplicate vm_map_destroy declarations in tests/vm_map_host.c that was breaking native builds.

📊 **Coverage:** What scenarios are now tested
- Finding a character with multiple occurrences (returns last)
- Finding the first character
- Finding the last character
- Finding a character not present (returns NULL)
- Finding the null terminator
- Handling empty strings (not found, and null terminator)

✨ **Result:** The improvement in test coverage
The strrchr function is now fully covered by tests across userland and kernel testing suites, catching edge cases and regressions.

